THOUGHT: NullAway complains because getMetadataDAO() is declared to return non-null but returns a @Nullable static field. Since callers likely expect a non-null DAO after initialization, the safest fix is to enforce non-null at access time by throwing if it hasn’t been initialized, rather than changing the return type to @Nullable. I’ll update getMetadataDAO() to check for null and throw an IllegalStateException if metadataDAO is null, then run the compile task to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/conductor && sed -i '32,34c\    public static MetadataDAO getMetadataDAO() {
        if (metadataDAO == null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("ValidationContext.metadataDAO has not been initialized");
        }
        return metadataDAO;
    }' core/src/main/java/com/netflix/conductor/validations/ValidationContext.java && ./gradlew conductor-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "ValidationContext" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

